00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.080
Hello?

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:13.280
Hello~?

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:14.500
HELLO!

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:16.400
Okay, sorry, didn't mean to do that.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:17.100
Hi!

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.520
Okay, goodbye!

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:20.800
Anybody here wanna fight? HUH?

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:23.140
Wanna fight with me br- OH! Heyy!

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:24.480
That guy just blew himself up!

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:25.680
Why did he do that?

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:26.760
AH!

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:29.220
Nononono~

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:32.480
This is a really cool bullet hell, I gotta admit because,

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.520
it's kinda stylistic in a great way

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:37.260
which I always like out of games. But also this one is just...

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:41.080
BONKERS in terms this, like, the ah, atmosphere of it.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.340
Like the music and like it all works together.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:43.840
Hep!

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:45.360
Cool, I got- I-

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:49.260
Okay, so tables are defensive structures, which are very handy.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.540
[unsympathetically] Oh no, poor guys.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:53.140
I got a blank. Good for me, no boss here.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:56.260
So I just need to scout out the rest of
dungeons until I find a boss

00:06:56.260 --> 00:07:00.040
and then I need to kick him in the ass until he gets an idea that I'm the boss now.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:00.900
Hup!

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:02.080
Not very clever when I say-

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:04.320
Oh, is that the boss? Oh.

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:06.380
[chuckles]

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:08.120
That's metal as fuck, bro.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.780
Hello! What? Are you the boss?

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:12.240
...You're the boss?

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:14.300
"You ready to put all you-" yeah, let's do it.

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:16.960
"Then... face me in si-" Ok.

